     },
     "body": "<p>Requesting that this please be closed <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" data-account-id=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" accountid=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Andrew Woods</a> in response to being contacted by <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=6089a48d248ef60073948d92\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"6089a48d248ef60073948d92\" data-account-id=\"6089a48d248ef60073948d92\" accountid=\"6089a48d248ef60073948d92\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Unknown</a> regarding the status of the issue, and confirming with both he and <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65\" data-account-id=\"5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65\" accountid=\"5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Esmé Cowles</a> that this would be indeed be best deprecated in favor of directing parties to use the new Java client.  Further, please note that the related PR (<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo4-client/pull/34\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo4-client/pull/34</a>) has been closed as well.</p>",
